From 895b3fd64fa1e58589acaa08598c455ec3a30aeb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: builder <builder@localhost>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 19:53:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 39/40] gatekeeper: build the gatekeeper@1.0 HAL for Huawei's
 TrustZone module

The 15.1 port set Huawei's TrustZone keystore and gatekeeper modules
aside (software keystore and gatekeeper). With qseecomd running they
work: the keymaster TrustZone app serves both. The keymaster@3.0 HAL
picks keystore.msm8937.so by itself; the gatekeeper HAL needs its
service again (installed and declared by stage A2 on the prebuilt
vendor).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 product/gatekeeper.mk | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 product/gatekeeper.mk

diff --git a/product/gatekeeper.mk b/product/gatekeeper.mk
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..892fb25
--- /dev/null
+++ b/product/gatekeeper.mk
@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@
+# Gatekeeper (lock screen credential checks) in TrustZone: Huawei's gatekeeper.msm8937.so talks to
+# the keymaster TrustZone app, which serves both. The 15.1 port had set the TrustZone modules aside
+# and used AOSP's software gatekeeper; with qseecomd running (init.ags_w09.tee.rc) they work.
+PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
+    android.hardware.gatekeeper@1.0-impl \
+    android.hardware.gatekeeper@1.0-service
-- 
